/-! # Order-`97` continuation of the `(8,10)` degree-one `π` tower

`Grok810PiSourceSplitScratch` leaves two live chambers after the
unsolved order-`96` head vanishes at a linear root of `h0`:

* LEFT: `v0 = s0 = q6 = u0 = w0 = 0` at `a`, tenth-face `M, T, G, V`,
  `F₁ ∨ F₂`, witnesses `m1, τ1, g1` with next-order laws, and `k1`
  the `Vred` quotient (`h0 ∣ Vred`);
* RIGHT: `t0 = u0 = w0 = v0 = s0 = q6 = 0` at `a`, the four scalar
  relations, and `u1 (5 v1² - 8 b62) = 0`.

The unsolved uniform quotient satisfies
`Head + h · Tail = C(η) · h¹⁶` from the source power relation.  This
file extracts the order-`97` coefficient (`h⁰` of `Tail`) — the first
order at which `m1, τ1, g1, k1` appear — and applies the remaining
power vanishing on both chambers and on the two right sub-branches.

The four scalar load solves are not inserted as polynomial identities.
The old scalar-solved `h⁹⁷` jet is not imported.  On the right
`u1 = 0` sibling the order-`97` mixin vanishes identically, so the
order-`96` head peels twice.  On the complementary factor the mixin
is a seven-term `λ u1` hypersurface.  Neither chamber is closed.

No total-degree or twice-prime theorem is used.
-/

noncomputable section

